== Source-role policy ==

* SEP and specialist philosophy literature: conceptual disputes and history of epistemic/scientific-method concepts.
* Primary/foundational papers: Gettier, Popper, Hempel/Oppenheim, etc.
* ISO/IEC/IEEE, NASA: engineering verification/validation.
* BIPM/JCGM and NIST: metrology, measurement uncertainty, accuracy/precision.
* W3C PROV: digital provenance.
* National Academies: reproducibility/replication convention.
* Wikipedia: title normalization, historical orientation, cross-link discovery.
* Scholarpedia: specialized technical descendants when directly relevant; no forced citations where direct coverage is absent.

== Reader linking rule ==

Core pages link to canonical Core titles.
Simple pages prefer <code>/Simple</code> where Wave 0 or Wave 1 provides it.
Technical pages prefer <code>/Technical</code> where available.

Redlinks are retained when the normalized prerequisite is useful; they are coverage signals, not automatic content-generation instructions.

